<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="49628" href="schedule/2014/fall/ARTS/299/49628.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120148" href="schedule/2014/fall.xml">Fall 2014</term><subject id="ARTS" href="schedule/2014/fall/ARTS.xml">Art--Studio</subject><course id="299" href="schedule/2014/fall/ARTS/299.xml">Spec Topics in Studio Art</course></parents><sectionNumber>PM1</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Intro to Printmaking</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Intro to Printmaking.  This course offers an introduction and overview of print processes including screenprint, intaglio, collagraph, and relief printmaking. Over the course of several projects that cumulatively build skills, students will gain familiarity with the ink lab facilities, printmaking best practices, and conceptual concerns unique to print media. Projects that relate to work developed in other studio and design areas will be encouraged.</sectionText><sectionFeeAmount>Printmaking Art Design $30.00 Flat Fee.</sectionFeeAmount><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-08-25Z</startDate><endDate>2014-12-10Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>12:10 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>7</roomNumber><buildingName>Noble Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Avery" firstName="M">Avery, M</instructor><instructor lastName="Lingscheit" firstName="E">Lingscheit, E</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>